# oracle: fix adapt 0 on pair lj/long/coul/long cut long 2.5 4.0 cut_coul (x 0.9, reset no) with kspace ewald: init_one's cutsq follows cut_coul, the Coulomb cutoff of init_style stays for the run; a second run initializes from the new cutoff
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12
units           lj
atom_style      charge
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 5 0 5 0 5
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            * 1.0
set             type 1 type/fraction 2 0.5 4321
variable        q atom 0.3*(2*(id%2)-1)
set             group all charge v_q
pair_style      lj/long/coul/long cut long 2.5 4.0
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 0.8 1.05
kspace_style    ewald 1.0e-4
velocity        all create 1.0 87287 loop geom
fix             1 all nve
variable        s equal 0.9
fix             2 all adapt 0 pair lj/long/coul/long cut_coul * * v_s scale yes reset no
thermo_style    custom step temp pe evdwl ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             20
run             20
